        <section type="header">
            <text>Chapter 21: The Progressive Era</text>
        </section>
        
        <section type="body">
            <paragraph id="1">
                <text>Progressive reformers established laws and institutions designed to improve working conditions, protect consumers, and regulate business practices. Key achievements included:</text>
            </paragraph>
            
            <list type="unordered">
                <item>The establishment of regulatory agencies</item>
                <item>Child labor laws</item>
                <item>Pure Food and Drug Act</item>
                <item>Women's suffrage movement</item>
            </list>
            
            <paragraph id="2">
                <text>These reforms fundamentally transformed American society and set the foundation for modern government regulation.</text>
            </paragraph>
        </section>
        
